+{id:'c2',ch:'code',type:'w',
+ q:'Walk through _clock_source_frequency() added by 701853d: what does each branch return, which single branch carries fault-profile drift, and what does the final raise protect against?',
+ snip:`<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_clock_source_frequency</span>(self, source: str) -> float:
+    <span class="kw">if</span> source == <span class="str">"DCO"</span>: <span class="kw">return</span> self._dco_actual()
+    <span class="kw">if</span> source == <span class="str">"LFXT"</span>: <span class="kw">return</span> self.clock.lfxt_frequency
+    <span class="kw">if</span> source == <span class="str">"HFXT"</span>: <span class="kw">return</span> self.clock.hfxt_frequency
+    <span class="kw">if</span> source == <span class="str">"VLO"</span>: <span class="kw">return</span> VLO_FREQUENCY_HZ
+    <span class="kw">if</span> source == <span class="str">"MODCLK"</span>: <span class="kw">return</span> MODCLK_FREQUENCY_HZ
+    <span class="kw">if</span> source == <span class="str">"LFMODCLK"</span>: <span class="kw">return</span> LFMODCLK_FREQUENCY_HZ
+    <span class="kw">raise</span> <span class="cls">ScpiError</span>(-<span class="num">221</span>, f<span class="str">"No simulated frequency for clock source {source}"</span>)`,
+ c:[{l:'DCO → _dco_actual() = dco_frequency × faults.dco_factor()',t:['_dco_actual','dco_factor','drift','× drift']},
+    {l:'LFXT/HFXT → the crystal fields on ClockState (32768 / 4e6 defaults)',t:['lfxt_frequency','hfxt_frequency','crystal','clockstate','32768']},
+    {l:'VLO/MODCLK/LFMODCLK → module constants 9400 / 4.8e6 / 37500',t:['9400','4.8e6','37500','constant','fixed']},
+    {l:'only the DCO branch is drift-affected',t:['only the dco','only dco','drift only','untouched','no drift']},
+    {l:'fallthrough raises -221 settings conflict — defends against unresolvable sources',t:['-221','raise','settings conflict','defensive','unknown','fallthrough']}],
+ m:`Branch by branch:
+- DCO → _dco_actual() = clock.dco_frequency × faults.dco_factor(). This is the ONLY drift-affected branch: NOMINAL profile returns ×1.0, CORNER applies the ±3.5% tolerance of SLASE54D.
+- LFXT → clock.lfxt_frequency (default 32768 — the watch crystal, a board property).
+- HFXT → clock.hfxt_frequency (default 4e6 — a documented simulator-only default, since real HFXT is whatever crystal the board fits).
+- VLO → VLO_FREQUENCY_HZ = 9400.0; MODCLK → MODCLK_FREQUENCY_HZ = 4.8e6; LFMODCLK → LFMODCLK_FREQUENCY_HZ = 4.8e6/128 = 37500. Fixed internal oscillators — no configuration register exists, so nothing to store.
+The final raise ScpiError(-221, "No simulated frequency for clock source …") is the same settings-conflict code the timer path uses for TACLK/INCLK (external inputs with no defined simulated frequency). Since the setters validate sources on the way in, this line is defensive — but it turns any future inconsistency (e.g. a new source added to the frozenset but not the resolver) into a loud queued error instead of a silently wrong number.`
