+{id:'s1',ch:'sil',type:'w',
+ q:'Describe the "lying frequency" failure mode: with MCLK switched to LFXT, what did the old CLOCK:MCLK:FREQUENCY? report versus reality, by what factor was it wrong, and why is a confidently wrong answer worse for SIL testing than an error?',
+ c:[{l:'old answer: 1000000 (DCO/1) regardless of selection',t:['1000000','1e6','1 mhz','dco/1','always dco']},
+    {l:'reality: 32768 (LFXT/1)',t:['32768']},
