+ m:`The firmware programs UCA0BRW = 1000000/9600 ≈ 104, believing SMCLK is the 1-MHz DCO. But SMCLK is actually VLO at ~9400 Hz, so the wire runs at 9400/104 ≈ 90 baud — roughly 106× slower than the intended 9600. Nothing meaningful ever arrives.
+Pre-fix, a SIL test that cross-checked the assumption — assert float(dev.process("CLOCK:SMCLK:FREQUENCY?")) == 1e6 — PASSED, because the old handler answered _dco_actual()/div regardless of the VLO selection. The simulator held the same false belief as the firmware; two matching errors cancel and the suite certifies broken code.
