+    {l:'fix 2: derive the expectation from queried state instead of a magic number',t:['derive','comput','query','function of','not a constant','magic number']}],
+ m:`Diagnosis: the expected "1000000" silently assumes SMCLK is still at its default route (DCO 1e6 / 1). Clock source and divider are device-level state that persist until changed or *RST. The other test selected MODCLK; with a shared device instance (or shared setup), this test now queries a 4.8-MHz SMCLK — the assertion was never really about SMCLK, it was about an unstated precondition. Note the failure only became POSSIBLE after 701853d: the old query ignored the source, so the leak was invisible — honest models surface hidden couplings.
