+- AVR: execution begins at flash 0x0000 (the "vector" is usually a JMP instruction). Harvard architecture — the vector is not even in the data address space.
+- 8051: execution begins at 0x0000.
+- x86: execution begins at physical 0xFFFFFFF0, which holds a far jump into firmware.
