+    {l:'new: load a firmware image\'s real vector via MEMORY:WRITE and assert reset lands on the entry point',t:['memory:write','entry point','vector','startup','lands']}],
+ m:`Bug class: FR5994 firmware parks big data (tables, logs) in extended FRAM at 0x10000-0x43FFF. A SIL script seeding a pointer register — CPU:REGISTER 9,0x28000 — got 0x28000 & 0xFFFF = 0x8000 stored: an address in the WRONG 64-KB page, with no error queued. Every downstream check ran against the wrong location.
