+{id:'i5',ch:'i2c',type:'mc',
+ q:'I2C0:FREQUENCY 12345 — what happens, and what was special about the OLD code here?',
+ opts:[
+  {t:'Rejected with -222; clock_frequency stays 100000. The old code had a dead "if v not in (...): pass" branch — validation that validated nothing',c:true, w:'Correct. Only the three real eUSCI_B modes exist: 100 kHz standard, 400 kHz fast, 1 MHz fast-plus. The old branch literally read "if v not in (100000, 400000, 1000000): pass  # Accept non-standard frequencies" — dead code the audit flagged as ACCEPTS_INVALID. The fix replaced pass with a -222 raise.'},
