+{id:'n3',ch:'int',type:'w',
+ q:'The audit calls 615b4e1 "minimal interrupt wiring." Describe precisely what IS modeled (state, gates, vectors) and what is deliberately NOT modeled, and connect the omission to the simulator\'s global caveat.',
+ c:[{l:'GIE stored (SR bit 3), set/clear via GIE/ENABLE/DISABLE, cleared on PUC',t:['gie','sr bit 3','eint','dint','cleared on','stored']},
+    {l:'VECTOR? = highest-priority pending source at real Table 9-4 addresses, gated by GIE',t:['table 9-4','priority','vector','gated','0xff']},
+    {l:'only GPIO P1-P8, TA0-2, TB0 tracked; other rows never contribute',t:['p1-p8','tb0','ta0','tracked','wdt, eusci','untracked','coverage']},
+    {l:'no asynchronous firing, no ISR entry — time does not pass',t:['time does not pass','asynchronous','never fires','no isr','on its own','dynamics']}],
+ m:`Modeled: GIE as real stored state — self._gie mirrors SR bit 3 (SLAU367P §4.3.3); INTERRUPT:GIE ON|OFF sets it, INTERRUPT:ENABLE/DISABLE mirror EINT/DINT, and _do_reset clears it (SR.GIE is cleared on a PUC — the WDT and interrupt commits meet here). INTERRUPT:VECTOR? walks _INTERRUPT_PRIORITY (TB0, TA0, TA1, P1, TA2, P2..P8 — real Table 9-4 order) and returns the first source whose enable AND flag are both set, at its real word address (TB0IV 0xFFF4, TAxIV 0xFFE8/0xFFE0/0xFFDA, P1..P8 0xFFDE..0xFFB6), gated by GIE; 0x0000 when gated or idle. INTERRUPT:FLAG? reports pending state ungated, matching real IFG semantics.
+Not modeled: every other Table 9-4 row (WDT, eUSCI_A/B, ADC12_B, DMA, RTC_C, AES, Comp_E, LEA, the NMIs) has no tracked enable/flag and never contributes; flags never fire asynchronously; no ISR is entered; nothing is cleared by "servicing".
+The omission follows the global caveat: time does not pass in the simulation. Flags reflect stored state that a test set explicitly — the same honesty as the watchdog that holds state but never expires. Configuration and pending-state are testable; dynamics are documented as out of scope rather than faked.`
+},
+
