+ q:'What do INTERRUPT:ENABLE and INTERRUPT:DISABLE do after 615b4e1?',
+ opts:[
+  {t:'Set and clear the stored GIE bit, mirroring __enable_interrupt()/EINT and __disable_interrupt()/DINT — before the commit they were no-ops and GIE was not even stored',c:true, w:'Correct. The audit\'s finding was "Stub — GIE state is not even stored." Now _int_enable does self._gie = True, _int_disable does self._gie = False, and INTERRUPT:GIE? reads the same bit that INTERRUPT:GIE ON|OFF writes — test_gie_stored exercises all four surfaces against one state.'},
+  {t:'Enable/disable a specific vector passed as a parameter',c:false,w:'Per-source enables live with the peripherals (e.g. GPIO:PORTn:INTERRUPT:ENABLE). The global commands model the single SR.GIE master gate.'},
+  {t:'They still do nothing; only INTERRUPT:GIE is wired',c:false,w:'All three write the same self._gie. ENABLE/DISABLE exist because firmware idiom is EINT/DINT — the test asserts ENABLE flips GIE? to "1" and DISABLE back to "0".'},
