+  <h1>Register Width and Encoding Constraints: Modeling What Silicon Can Actually Hold</h1>
+  <p class="tagline">Why this matters: a Python int can hold 0x12345, but the 16-bit TAxR register it models cannot. Until commit a20fbb1 the MSP430 timer model accepted values, dividers, and register states that no silicon can reach — and every SIL test built on those states was silently void.</p>
