+  <h1>Clock Trees: Why Reported Frequency Must Follow the Selected Source</h1>
+  <p class="tagline">Why this matters: a clock signal is a source routed through a divider, not a stored number. Until commit 701853d the MSP430 model answered <code>CLOCK:MCLK:FREQUENCY?</code> from the DCO no matter which source was selected — silently lying to every timer interval and baud calculation downstream.</p>
+</header>
