+{id:'a5',ch:'alias',type:'w',
+ q:'probe_gpio_pull_both: quote (approximately) its return expression before and after 4cb71a1, and explain what flipping the expected value means for how audit probes are written.',
+ c:[{l:'before: pullup &amp; pulldown &amp; 0x01 == 0x01 (both active = bug reproduced)',t:['== 0x01','both','reproduc','demonstrat']},
+    {l:'after: pullup &amp; pulldown &amp; 0x01 == 0 (mutually exclusive)',t:['== 0','mutual','exclusive']},
+    {l:'same stimulus (PULLUP 0x01; PULLDOWN 0x01) both times',t:['same command','same stimulus','same sequence','0x01']},
+    {l:'probes assert the compliant behaviour, so they flip when fixed',t:['compliant','assert the correct','docstring','flip','sla','12.2.4']}],
+ m:`Stimulus (unchanged): dev.process("GPIO:PORT1:PULLUP 0x01"); dev.process("GPIO:PORT1:PULLDOWN 0x01").
+Before: return dev.ports[1].pullup & dev.ports[1].pulldown & 0x01 == 0x01 — docstring "Pull-up and pull-down can be enabled simultaneously on one pin." The probe returned True when the BUG was present, documenting the non-compliance.
+After: return dev.ports[1].pullup & dev.ports[1].pulldown & 0x01 == 0 — docstring "Pull-up and pull-down are mutually exclusive on one pin (one PxREN bit)."
+The convention this shows: audit probes always encode the behaviour SLAU367P specifies for the current verdict. While a finding is open, the probe verifies the defect is still reproducible (so the report can't go stale); when the fix lands, the probe and docstring flip to assert compliance and become a permanent regression guard. Same stimulus, opposite expectation — the diff of the probe IS the specification of the fix.`
+},
