+// ─── CHANNEL: input ───────────────────────────────────────────
+{id:'i1',ch:'input',type:'w',
+ q:'Reproduce the body of _gpio_inp after 4cb71a1 (four mask lines plus the OR). For each term, say which class of pin it captures and which register wins there.',
+ c:[{l:'driven = output &amp; direction (output pins read back OUT)',t:['output & direction','out & dir','driven']},
+    {l:'undriven_mask = ~direction &amp; 0xFF',t:['~direction','~dir','undriven']},
+    {l:'pulled = output &amp; resistor_enable &amp; undriven (REN input pins read the pull level = OUT bit)',t:['resistor_enable','ren','pull level','pulled']},
+    {l:'injected = input &amp; undriven &amp; ~resistor_enable (no-pull input pins read injection)',t:['~resistor','~ren','inject']},
+    {l:'effective = driven | pulled | injected',t:['driven | pulled','or','union','effective']}],
+ m:`driven        = p.output & p.direction
+undriven_mask = ~p.direction & 0xFF
+pulled        = p.output & p.resistor_enable & undriven_mask
+injected      = p.input & undriven_mask & ~p.resistor_enable
+effective     = driven | pulled | injected      # returned as f"0x{effective & 0xFF:02X}"
+Three disjoint pin classes, each owned by one source:
+1. Output pins (DIR=1): read back PxOUT — "driven".
+2. Input pins with a pull (DIR=0, REN=1): read PxOUT's bit too, but with a different meaning — it is the pull level (0=pulled low, 1=pulled high). This is the pull-aware read §12.2.4 requires.
+3. Input pins without a pull (DIR=0, REN=0): read the externally injected value, as before the commit.
+The masks partition all 8 pins, so the OR never double-assigns a bit. Note injected is masked by ~resistor_enable: on a REN pin the pull always wins because the model has no drive-strength arbitration.`
+},
+
+{id:'i2',ch:'input',type:'mc',
+ q:'direction = 0xF0, output = 0xA5, resistor_enable = 0x0C, injected input = 0x03. What does GPIO:PORT1:INPUT? return?',
+ snip:`driven   = OUT &amp; DIR
+undriven = ~DIR &amp; 0xFF
+pulled   = OUT &amp; REN &amp; undriven
+injected = IN &amp; undriven &amp; ~REN
+<span class="kw">return</span> driven | pulled | injected`,
+ opts:[
+  {t:'0xA7',c:true, w:'Correct. driven = 0xA5 &amp; 0xF0 = 0xA0. undriven = 0x0F. pulled = 0xA5 &amp; 0x0C &amp; 0x0F = 0x04 (pin 2 pull-up reads 1; pin 3 pull-down reads 0). injected = 0x03 &amp; 0x0F &amp; ~0x0C = 0x03. 0xA0 | 0x04 | 0x03 = 0xA7.'},
+  {t:'0xA3',c:false,w:'0xA3 = driven | injected only — that is the PRE-4cb71a1 result, which ignored pulls. Pin 2\'s pull-up (REN bit 2, OUT bit 2 = 1) adds 0x04.'},
+  {t:'0xA5',c:false,w:'0xA5 is OUT itself. OUT only shows through fully on output pins (high nibble); on the input nibble only the REN-enabled bits of OUT appear (0x04), the rest comes from injection.'},
+  {t:'0x07',c:false,w:'0x07 drops the driven high nibble. Output pins read back OUT &amp; DIR = 0xA0 — PxIN reflects driven levels too.'},
+ ]
+},
+
+{id:'i3',ch:'input',type:'mc',
+ q:'The flipped audit probe: DIRECTION 0x00, RESISTOR:ENABLE 0xFF, OUTPUT 0xFF — what must INPUT? return for probe_gpio_input_ignores_pulls to report compliance?',
+ opts:[
+  {t:'"0xFF" — every pin is an undriven input with an enabled pull-up, so every pin reads high',c:true, w:'Correct. pulled = OUT &amp; REN &amp; undriven = 0xFF &amp; 0xFF &amp; 0xFF = 0xFF. Before the fix the same setup (via PULLUP 0xFF) returned "0x00" because reads ignored pulls entirely — the PARTIAL finding on GPIO:PORTn:INPUT.'},
+  {t:'"0x00" — input pins with no injected value always read low',c:false,w:'That was the OLD, non-compliant behaviour. §12.2.4: an undriven input with a pull-up reads high — the whole point of the resistor.'},
+  {t:'Whatever was last injected with GPIO:PORT1:INPUT',c:false,w:'Injection is masked out on REN-enabled pins (injected = IN &amp; undriven &amp; ~REN). With REN = 0xFF, injection is invisible.'},
+  {t:'An error — OUTPUT writes are illegal while all pins are inputs',c:false,w:'Writing PxOUT on input pins is not only legal, it is HOW you select pull direction (Table 12-1). No error is queued.'},
+ ]
+},
