+{id:'i4',ch:'input',type:'mc',
+ q:'Pin 3 is an input with REN set and OUT bit 3 = 0 (pull-down). A test sends GPIO:PORT1:INPUT 0x08, injecting a high on pin 3. What does INPUT? bit 3 read?',
+ opts:[
+  {t:'0 — the injected bit is masked by ~resistor_enable; on a REN pin the pull level always wins because the model has no drive-strength arbitration',c:true, w:'Correct. injected = IN &amp; undriven &amp; ~REN kills bit 3; pulled = OUT &amp; REN &amp; undriven contributes OUT bit 3 = 0. Real hardware would let a strong external driver overpower the weak pull — Silmulator deliberately does not model drive strength, so simulating "external device overrides the pull" requires clearing that pin\'s REN bit for the duration.'},
+  {t:'1 — injection models an external driver, which overpowers a weak pull',c:false,w:'That is what real silicon does, but not this model: _gpio_inp masks injection with ~resistor_enable. Know the divergence before writing button/press tests.'},
+  {t:'1 — the injection write also sets OUT bit 3',c:false,w:'GPIO:PORTn:INPUT writes only p.input (the injected value); it never touches output or resistor_enable.'},
+  {t:'SCPI error -221 — injecting onto a pulled pin is a settings conflict',c:false,w:'No error is queued; the injected value is simply not visible while REN is set on that pin.'},
+ ]
+},
