+{id:'i5',ch:'input',type:'w',
+ q:'SIL test for an active-low button on P1.3 with an internal pull-up: give the SCPI configuration, the expected idle read, and the sequence that simulates a press — including why plain injection is not enough.',
+ c:[{l:'config: PIN:DIRECTION 3,INPUT + RESISTOR:ENABLE 0x08 + OUTPUT 0x08',t:['0x08','resistor:enable','output 0x08','direction 3']},
+    {l:'idle: INPUT? bit 3 reads 1 (pull-up)',t:['reads 1','bit 3 = 1','high','0x08']},
+    {l:'injection of 0 is masked while REN is set (~resistor_enable)',t:['masked','ignored','~ren','~resistor','pull wins','not enough']},
+    {l:'press: clear REN (RESISTOR:ENABLE 0x00), inject 0, read 0; restore after',t:['clear ren','resistor:enable 0x00','disable','restore','re-enable']}],
+ m:`Idle configuration (matches firmware P1DIR &= ~BIT3; P1REN |= BIT3; P1OUT |= BIT3):
+GPIO:PORT1:PIN:DIRECTION 3,INPUT
+GPIO:PORT1:RESISTOR:ENABLE 0x08
+GPIO:PORT1:OUTPUT 0x08
+GPIO:PORT1:INPUT?              → bit 3 = 1 (pulled : 0x08 &amp; 0x08 &amp; undriven) — unpressed reads high. ✓
+Simulating the press: GPIO:PORT1:INPUT 0x00 alone does NOT work — injected = IN & undriven & ~REN, so pin 3's injection is masked while its REN bit is set; INPUT? still shows 1. The model treats REN pins as undriven (no drive-strength arbitration), whereas a real button is a hard short to GND that overpowers the ~35 kΩ pull.
+Workaround: model the press as "strong driver replaces the pull" —
+GPIO:PORT1:RESISTOR:ENABLE 0x00   (disconnect the resistor for the press)
+GPIO:PORT1:INPUT 0x00             → INPUT? bit 3 = 0 — press observed
+…and restore RESISTOR:ENABLE 0x08 (and re-inject) on release. Document the divergence if the firmware under test reads PxREN itself.`
+},
