+{id:'v1',ch:'valid',type:'mc',
+ q:'A test sends GPIO:PORT1:PIN:VALUE 12,1. Per the flipped probe, what is the device state afterwards?',
+ snip:`<span class="cm"># scripts/audit_msp430.py — AFTER 4cb71a1</span>
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">probe_gpio_pin_index_unvalidated</span>(dev):
+    <span class="str">"""Pin numbers beyond 7 are rejected with -222 on an 8-bit port."""</span>
+    dev.process(<span class="str">"GPIO:PORT1:PIN:VALUE 12,1"</span>)
+    <span class="kw">return</span> _errors(dev) == <span class="num">1</span> <span class="kw">and</span> dev.ports[<span class="num">1</span>].output == <span class="num">0</span>`,
+ opts:[
+  {t:'One SCPI error (-222, "Pin index out of range (0-7): 12") is queued and output is untouched at 0',c:true, w:'Correct. _validate_pin raises before any shift or mutation happens — validate-then-mutate. The probe asserts BOTH halves: exactly one error, and no state corruption.'},
+  {t:'Bit 12 is set: output becomes 0x1000',c:false,w:'That was the OLD behaviour — (1 &lt;&lt; 12) stored into an "8-bit" register, corrupting every later mask read. The audit called it ACCEPTS_INVALID.'},
+  {t:'The index wraps modulo 8, setting pin 4',c:false,w:'No wrapping. A pin that does not exist is an error, not a remapping — SLAU367P §12.2: each port has exactly 8 I/O lines.'},
+  {t:'Error -224 is queued — illegal parameter value',c:false,w:'-224 is for tokens outside a permitted value SET (like PIN:DIRECTION 0,BANANA). A numeric index outside its RANGE is -222, "Data out of range".'},
+ ]
+},
+
+{id:'v2',ch:'valid',type:'mc',
+ q:'Why does pin 12 draw error -222 but PIN:DIRECTION 0,BANANA draw -224?',
+ opts:[
+  {t:'-222 "Data out of range" = right type, numeric value outside 0-7; -224 "Illegal parameter value" = token outside the permitted value set (a pin is INPUT or OUTPUT, no third mode)',c:true, w:'Correct. Same split as elsewhere in the model: register-width violations use -222 (lesson 0010\'s timer writes), value-set violations use -224 (ADC:REFERENCE BANANA, divider /128). The SCPI error class encodes WHY the parameter is unacceptable.'},
+  {t:'They are interchangeable; the codes were picked arbitrarily per handler',c:false,w:'They follow the SCPI standard\'s classification and the codebase\'s existing precedent — numeric range vs value-set membership.'},
+  {t:'-222 is a warning, -224 halts command processing',c:false,w:'Both queue an error and leave state unchanged; neither halts anything. The difference is meaning, not severity.'},
+  {t:'BANANA fails integer parsing, which is always -224',c:false,w:'Type/parse failures are the -1xx family (e.g. -104 for the VEREF voltage). BANANA parses fine as a token — it is simply not in {INPUT, OUTPUT, IN, OUT, 0, 1}.'},
+ ]
+},
+
+{id:'v3',ch:'valid',type:'w',
+ q:'Write _validate_pin from memory (decorator, signature, check, error), and state which handlers call it and at what point in their flow.',
+ c:[{l:'@staticmethod, takes pin: int, returns None',t:['staticmethod','pin: int','none']},
+    {l:'if not 0 <= pin <= 7 → raise',t:['0 <= pin <= 7','0-7','not 0','chained']},
+    {l:'ScpiError(-222, "Pin index out of range (0-7): {pin}")',t:['-222','out of range']},
+    {l:'called by _gpio_pin_dir and _gpio_pin_val, right after parsing, before any read or mutation',t:['pin_dir','pin_val','before','both','first','prior to']}],
+ m:`@staticmethod
+def _validate_pin(pin: int) -> None:
+    """Reject pin indexes outside an 8-bit port's 8 I/O lines (SLAU367P §12.2)."""
+    if not 0 <= pin <= 7:
+        raise ScpiError(-222, f"Pin index out of range (0-7): {pin}")
+It is a @staticmethod because it touches no instance state — pure validation. Both per-pin handlers call it immediately after pin = int(cmd.params[0]) and before anything else: _gpio_pin_dir (which also gained the -224 rejection for illegal mode strings) and _gpio_pin_val. Placement matters: the check runs before the query branch AND before any (1 << pin) shift, so neither reads nor writes can ever touch a nonexistent line — rejection leaves state exactly as it was (the probe asserts output == 0 afterwards). One shared validator, two call sites: the range rule lives in one place.`
+},
