+<section>
+<h2>3. The Fix — What Commit 701853d Actually Changed</h2>
+
+<p>Issue #20 came out of the MSP430 compliance audit. Five clock probes flagged the same theme: the model stored clock configuration but neither validated it against the FR5994's real encodings nor <em>used</em> it when answering frequency queries.</p>
+
+<h3>Before: FREQUENCY? hardwired to one oscillator per clock</h3>
+<pre><code><span class="cm"># silmulator/devices/msp430.py — BEFORE 701853d</span>
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_clk_mclk_freq</span>(self, cmd: <span class="cls">ScpiCommand</span>) -> str:
+    <span class="del">freq = self._dco_actual() / self.clock.mclk_div</span>      <span class="cm"># ← always DCO</span>
+    <span class="kw">return</span> f<span class="str">"{freq:.0f}"</span>
+
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_clk_aclk_freq</span>(self, cmd: <span class="cls">ScpiCommand</span>) -> str:
+    <span class="del">freq = self.clock.lfxt_frequency / self.clock.aclk_div</span> <span class="cm"># ← always LFXT</span>
+    <span class="kw">return</span> f<span class="str">"{freq:.0f}"</span></code></pre>
+
+<p>The source-select commands <em>stored</em> the selection (<code>self.clock.mclk_source = v</code>) but the query never read it back. SMCLK's source and all SMCLK/ACLK dividers were not validated at all (<code>CLOCK:SMCLK:SOURCE BANANA</code> succeeded), MCLK's validation set wrongly contained REFO and DCOCLKDIV, and dividers allowed /64 and /128.</p>
+
+<h3>After: one resolver walks the tree</h3>
+<pre><code><span class="cm"># silmulator/devices/msp430.py — AFTER 701853d</span>
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_clock_source_frequency</span>(self, source: str) -> float:
+    <span class="str">"""Effective frequency (Hz) of one clock-system source, pre-divider.
+
+    SLAU367P §3.2: DCO is the drift-affected trimmed oscillator
+    (``_dco_actual()``); LFXT/HFXT read the crystal fields on
+    ``ClockState``; VLO and MODCLK are fixed-frequency internal
+    oscillators with no configurable register; LFMODCLK is MODCLK/128.
+    """</span>
+    <span class="kw">if</span> source == <span class="str">"DCO"</span>:
+        <span class="kw">return</span> self._dco_actual()          <span class="cm"># dco_frequency × fault-profile drift</span>
+    <span class="kw">if</span> source == <span class="str">"LFXT"</span>:
+        <span class="kw">return</span> self.clock.lfxt_frequency   <span class="cm"># 32768 default</span>
+    <span class="kw">if</span> source == <span class="str">"HFXT"</span>:
+        <span class="kw">return</span> self.clock.hfxt_frequency   <span class="cm"># 4e6 simulator-only default</span>
+    <span class="kw">if</span> source == <span class="str">"VLO"</span>:
+        <span class="kw">return</span> VLO_FREQUENCY_HZ            <span class="cm"># 9400.0 — fixed, no register</span>
+    <span class="kw">if</span> source == <span class="str">"MODCLK"</span>:
+        <span class="kw">return</span> MODCLK_FREQUENCY_HZ         <span class="cm"># 4.8e6 — fixed, no register</span>
+    <span class="kw">if</span> source == <span class="str">"LFMODCLK"</span>:
+        <span class="kw">return</span> LFMODCLK_FREQUENCY_HZ       <span class="cm"># MODCLK / 128 = 37500</span>
+    <span class="kw">raise</span> <span class="cls">ScpiError</span>(-<span class="num">221</span>, f<span class="str">"No simulated frequency for clock source {source}"</span>)
+
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_clk_mclk_freq</span>(self, cmd: <span class="cls">ScpiCommand</span>) -> str:
+    <span class="add">freq = self._clock_source_frequency(self.clock.mclk_source) / self.clock.mclk_div</span>
+    <span class="kw">return</span> f<span class="str">"{freq:.0f}"</span>   <span class="cm"># SMCLK and ACLK queries are the same shape</span></code></pre>
+
+<h3>Validation now mirrors the register encodings</h3>
+<pre><code><span class="cm"># CSCTL2.SELM/SELS: MCLK and SMCLK share one source mux. REFO and DCOCLKDIV</span>
+<span class="cm"># have no encoding on the FR59xx CS; MODCLK and LFMODCLK do.</span>
+VALID_MCLK_SMCLK_SOURCES = <span class="fn">frozenset</span>({<span class="str">"LFXT"</span>, <span class="str">"VLO"</span>, <span class="str">"LFMODCLK"</span>, <span class="str">"DCO"</span>, <span class="str">"MODCLK"</span>, <span class="str">"HFXT"</span>})
+<span class="cm"># CSCTL2.SELA: ACLK's source mux is a narrower subset of the above.</span>
+VALID_ACLK_SOURCES = <span class="fn">frozenset</span>({<span class="str">"LFXT"</span>, <span class="str">"VLO"</span>, <span class="str">"LFMODCLK"</span>})
+<span class="cm"># CSCTL3.DIVM/DIVS/DIVA: all three dividers share the same 3-bit, power-of-two</span>
+<span class="cm"># encoding that tops out at /32 (values above /32 have no encoding).</span>
+VALID_CLOCK_DIVIDERS = <span class="fn">frozenset</span>({<span class="num">1</span>, <span class="num">2</span>, <span class="num">4</span>, <span class="num">8</span>, <span class="num">16</span>, <span class="num">32</span>})</code></pre>
+
+<p>Every setter now checks its set before storing — a bad source raises <code>ScpiError(-224, "Illegal clock source: …")</code>, a bad divider raises <code>ScpiError(-222, "Illegal divider: …")</code>, and in both cases <strong>the previous state is left unchanged</strong>. Note the divider error code <em>changed</em> from -224 to -222: a divider is numeric data outside the representable range (-222, "Data out of range"), while a source token outside the enum is an illegal parameter value (-224).</p>
+
+<h3>The timer path was fixed the same way</h3>
+<pre><code><span class="cm"># _timer_tick_frequency — timers now see the real tree, not a hardwired source</span>
+<span class="kw">if</span> ts.clock_source == <span class="str">"SMCLK"</span>:
+    <span class="del">src = self._dco_actual() / self.clock.smclk_div</span>
+    <span class="add">src = self._clock_source_frequency(self.clock.smclk_source) / self.clock.smclk_div</span>
+<span class="kw">elif</span> ts.clock_source == <span class="str">"ACLK"</span>:
+    <span class="del">src = self.clock.lfxt_frequency / self.clock.aclk_div</span>
+    <span class="add">src = self._clock_source_frequency(self.clock.aclk_source) / self.clock.aclk_div</span></code></pre>
+
+<h3>Tests flipped from expected-failure to passing</h3>
+<p>Two audit-derived tests dropped their <code>@pytest.mark.xfail(strict=True)</code> decorators, becoming permanent regression guards:</p>
+<pre><code><span class="cm"># tests/test_msp430_edge_cases.py — AFTER 701853d (xfail decorators removed)</span>
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">test_mclk_divider_64_rejected</span>(self, mcu):
+    <span class="cm"># SLAU367P §3.3.3: DIVM encodings stop at /32.</span>
+    mcu.process(<span class="str">"CLOCK:MCLK:DIVIDER 64"</span>)
+    <span class="kw">assert</span> <span class="fn">errors</span>(mcu) == <span class="num">1</span>
+
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">test_mclk_source_modclk_accepted</span>(self, mcu):
+    <span class="cm"># SLAU367P §3.3.2 (CSCTL2.SELM): MODCLK is encoding 4.</span>
+    mcu.process(<span class="str">"CLOCK:MCLK:SOURCE MODCLK"</span>)</code></pre>
+
+<p>Five audit probes were rescored, including the headline one — <code>probe_mclk_freq_ignores_source</code> now asserts that an LFXT-sourced MCLK reads <code>lfxt_frequency / mclk_div</code>, the compliant behaviour, instead of documenting the DCO lie.</p>
+</section>
+
