+    <div class="feedback"></div>
+  </div>
+
+  <!-- Q2 -->
+  <div class="question" data-question>
+    <p class="q-text"><span class="q-num">Q2.</span> A test sends <code>CLOCK:MCLK:SOURCE REFO</code>. What happens, and why?</p>
+    <ul class="options">
+      <li data-correct="true"  data-why="REFO is a UCS-module source on F5xx/6xx parts; the FR59xx CS module has no SELM encoding for it. It is not in VALID_MCLK_SMCLK_SOURCES, so _clk_mclk_src raises ScpiError(-224) and mclk_source is left unchanged.">SCPI error -224 is queued and the previous source is kept — REFO has no CSCTL2.SELM encoding on the FR5994</li>
+      <li data-correct="false" data-why="That was the pre-701853d behaviour: the old VALID set wrongly contained REFO (and DCOCLKDIV) while rejecting MODCLK — backwards for this chip.">The source is set to REFO; it was valid before the fix and stays valid</li>
+      <li data-correct="false" data-why="-222 is for numeric data out of range — the divider path. A token outside the enumerated source set draws -224, Illegal parameter value.">SCPI error -222 is queued</li>
+      <li data-correct="false" data-why="No coercion happens anywhere in the clock handlers. Validation is a strict membership test against the frozenset; rejection leaves state untouched.">The model substitutes the nearest equivalent source (LFXT)</li>
+    </ul>
+    <div class="feedback"></div>
+  </div>
+
+  <!-- Q3 -->
+  <div class="question" data-question>
+    <p class="q-text"><span class="q-num">Q3.</span> Why does <code>CLOCK:ACLK:SOURCE DCO</code> fail while <code>CLOCK:SMCLK:SOURCE DCO</code> succeeds?</p>
